# The first-launch empty state: OSM Carto is already on the map and a welcome
# card says what to do. No `viewport` op is used before the first capture of
# the default view, so this shows the real startup state.
#
# The map area is 864x776 with its origin at window (56, 0), so its centre is
# window (488, 388). The card sits near the bottom centre of the map.

window 1200 800
wait 3s
wait_idle 5s
# Default viewport: too large an area for the OSM API, so the card shows
# "Zoom in to download" instead of a button.
capture out/empty-default.png

# Zoomed out further: still "Zoom in to download".
viewport 40.7128 -74.0060 8
wait_idle 5s
capture out/empty-zoomed-out.png

# Zoomed in far enough to download: the button is enabled.
viewport 40.7128 -74.0060 16
wait_idle 5s
capture out/empty-zoomed-in.png

# The card does not block the map: a pan-drag across the map (and over the
# card) still moves it.
drag 700,200 500,350
wait_idle 5s
capture out/empty-panned.png

# Once data is loaded the card goes away.
load_osm docs/screenshots/fixtures/select.osm
viewport 40.7120 -74.0060 18
wait_idle 5s
capture out/empty-data-loaded.png
